        "example": "Consider an enterprise border firewall inspecting high-speed TLS SNI (Server Name Indication) extensions and DNS query payloads across 40 Gbps network interfaces. The intrusion prevention system must identify malicious domain signatures, such as 'malware-c2-command.org', embedded within gigabytes of transit packets. If the firewall used a backtracking pattern matcher, an adversary could stream repetitive decoy payloads like 'malware-c2-com...malware-c2-com...' designed to trigger worst-case quadratic backtracking, saturating firewall CPU cores and dropping benign traffic. By deploying the zero-backtrack KMP engine, the firewall processes each packet in linear time, guaranteeing constant per-byte latency and immunizing the infrastructure against algorithmic denial-of-service exploits.",
